message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
title: "Two-coordinate obstructions for affine interpretations of the Yolcu–Aaronson–Heule Collatz system"
authors:
  - family-names: Valbuena
    given-names: Lucas
repository-code: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
url: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
abstract: >-
  Lean proofs and a paper showing that nonnegative real affine interpretations
  in two coordinates, with first diagonal entry at least one for every symbol,
  have zero first-coordinate offset gap for every rule whenever all eleven
  rules of the Yolcu–Aaronson–Heule Collatz system are weakly oriented
  coefficientwise. The result holds separately for the original system and
  its word reversal. A second theorem removes the diagonal bounds for the
  reversed system: all eleven weak comparisons force equality of the full
  offset vectors in both eligible TOP rules, da to d and db to dg.
  Section 9 gives an independent second proof of Omar Javier Said Duran’s
  theorem on arbitrarily long consecutive runs with equal finite Collatz
  height and equal odd-step counts. Priority belongs to his earlier preprint,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.23003526. The finite-pattern formulation is equivalent.
  Section 10 gives analytic deductions from Tao's first-passage stabilization:
  logarithmic basin densities, total-variation limits of countable orbit labels,
  a fixed-target odd-step time law, and equality of the critical Green and
  cylinder Cesaro and Abel limits at every positive integer. A counting
  argument determines the optimal exponential rate of the largest stationary
  cylinder mass. Section 10 is
  not included in the Lean formalization.
  These results do not prove the Collatz conjecture.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - string rewriting
  - matrix interpretations
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - logarithmic density
  - first passage
